hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-14 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-14 = cons (quoted (cons "*Social* comes from *socius*, a companion, from the root " (cons "to follow" (cons ". The modern platforms call people " (cons "followers" (cons ", which is exactly the root. But *socius* was the one who walks beside you, an ally, not the one who walks behind. The platforms kept the root and reversed the posture. Interpersonal computing restores *socius*: networks of companions, side by side, in fields where everyone navigates and no one only follows." nil)))))) (cons "" (cons "*Communicate* is from *communis*, shared, whose root holds *munus*, a gift and a duty, from the root for exchange. Making common is giving and owing at once. *Community*, *municipal*, *immunity* (exemption from the duty) all come from it. Communicating with intention is exchanging gifts while stretching toward each other. Collaboration in its true sense is gift exchange between people reaching for one another, which is a better account of an open-source commons than any economic model." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "*Free*, from the root meaning " (cons "beloved, one's own" (cons ", is the same word as *friend*. The free person was the beloved member of the household. Giving everything for free — technoanarchocommunism — is in the roots of the words the economy of the beloved: what friends give one another. Gift (*munus*), friend (*free*), companion (*socius*), and kin (*kind*) are the four pillars of that non-market economy." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "*Slave*, through Medieval Latin *sclavus*, is the name of the Slavs, captured and sold in the early Middle Ages. Slavic *slovo* means word. The people of the word became the word for unfree. *Infant* is *in* + *fans*, not speaking. So unfreedom and unspeech are tied in the words twice. Disinhibited speech is the direct path to truth. *Inhibit* is *in* + *habere*, to hold in. Disinhibition is releasing what was held in: the slave's word released, the infant learning to speak. The human superorganism in its infancy is, by the word, a species that hasn't learned to speak yet." (cons "" (cons "*Category* is the speaking-against in the assembly, *kata* + *agoreuein*. To categorize was to accuse in public. Fields that agree on what to be ignorant about are categories in that sense: accusations that became walls. *Concept* is *con* + *capere*, taken together; *comprehend* is *com* + *prehendere*, grasped together. *Abstract* is *abs* + *trahere*, drawn away. Abstraction is literally a drawing-away from the thing. Collapsing false disciplinary distinctions undoes the category's accusation and pulls the abstraction back to what it was drawn from." (cons "" nil)))))))))
